Subject: inputmethod/anthy-elisp: accept emacs26 through emacs30
From: zakinko@snowrabbit.org
Reply-To: zakinko@snowrabbit.org
X-send-pr-version: 3.95

>Submitter-Id:	net
>Originator:	Showta Ishizaki
>Organization:
>Confidential:	no
>Synopsis:	inputmethod/anthy-elisp: accept emacs26 through emacs30
>Severity:	non-critical
>Priority:	low
>Category:	pkg
>Class:		change-request
>Release:	NetBSD 11.0, pkgsrc trunk fa7ad771c96929bf742033e6ccfd8bb45b9cab49
>Environment:
System: NetBSD 11.0 i386
Architecture: i386
Machine: i386
>Description:
	inputmethod/anthy-elisp only accepts emacs21, emacs20 and XEmacs:

	  EMACS_VERSIONS_ACCEPTED= emacs21 emacs21nox emacs20 \
	                           xemacs215 xemacs215nox xemacs214 xemacs214nox

	so on a machine with a current Emacs it stops in can-be-built-here.mk:

	  ERROR: Accepted versions are: emacs21 emacs21nox emacs20 xemacs215 ...
	  ERROR: No valid Emacs version installed found

	That line has not changed since the package was last restructured,
	while the Makefile itself has been touched as recently as 2024, so it
	looks like nobody has tried a newer Emacs rather than a known
	incompatibility.

	This matters because anthy-elisp is the only package that installs
	anthy.el (apart from the tamago ones).  An init file that does

	  (load-library "anthy")
	  (setq default-input-method 'japanese-anthy)

	therefore has no way to work on any Emacs newer than 21 through
	pkgsrc.

>How-To-Repeat:
	env EMACS_TYPE=emacs26nox make -C /usr/pkgsrc/inputmethod/anthy-elisp fetch

	  ERROR: [can-be-built-here.mk] This package has PKG_FAIL_REASON set:
	  ERROR: Accepted versions are: emacs21 emacs21nox emacs20 xemacs215 ...
	  ERROR: No valid Emacs version installed found

>Fix:
	Add emacs26 through emacs30 to EMACS_VERSIONS_ACCEPTED.  PKGREVISION is
	left alone: the installed files do not change, only which Emacs the
	package will build against.

	Built and packaged on NetBSD 11.0/i386 with EMACS_TYPE=emacs26nox.
	Byte compilation of src-util/*.el completes and the package installs
	as anthy-elisp-9100hnb6, with six .elc files.

	Note that anthy.el still refers to last-command-char, which was removed
	in Emacs 26; users work around it with

	  (define-obsolete-variable-alias 'last-command-char 'last-command-event ...)

	in their init file.  Byte compilation only warns about it, so the
	package builds, but it would be worth patching properly if you would
	rather carry the fix in pkgsrc.

	I have not been able to confirm emacs30nox yet: editors/emacs30-nox11
	builds emacs30-nox11-30.2, but editors/emacs/modules.mk asks for
	emacs30-no-x11>=30.1<31, and the build stops with

	  ERROR: [depends.mk] A package matching ``emacs30-no-x11>=30.1<31''
	  ERROR:     should be installed, but one cannot be found.

	That looks like a separate problem in the emacs30 packages, not in
	this one.

	Index: inputmethod/anthy-elisp/Makefile
	===================================================================
	RCS file: /cvsroot/pkgsrc/inputmethod/anthy-elisp/Makefile,v
	retrieving revision 1.14
	diff -u -r1.14 Makefile
	--- inputmethod/anthy-elisp/Makefile	8 May 2024 12:20:52 -0000	1.14
	+++ inputmethod/anthy-elisp/Makefile	14 Aug 2026 15:13:45 -0000
	@@ -14,7 +14,13 @@
	 CONFIGURE_ENV+=	EMACS=${EMACS_BIN:Q}
	 EMACS_MODULES+=	base leim
	 
	-EMACS_VERSIONS_ACCEPTED=	emacs21 emacs21nox emacs20 xemacs215 xemacs215nox xemacs214 xemacs214nox
	+EMACS_VERSIONS_ACCEPTED=	emacs21 emacs21nox emacs20
	+EMACS_VERSIONS_ACCEPTED+=	xemacs215 xemacs215nox xemacs214 xemacs214nox
	+EMACS_VERSIONS_ACCEPTED+=	emacs26 emacs26nox
	+EMACS_VERSIONS_ACCEPTED+=	emacs27 emacs27nox
	+EMACS_VERSIONS_ACCEPTED+=	emacs28 emacs28nox
	+EMACS_VERSIONS_ACCEPTED+=	emacs29 emacs29nox
	+EMACS_VERSIONS_ACCEPTED+=	emacs30 emacs30nox
	 
	 .include "../../editors/emacs/modules.mk"
	 
